the dynamic memory allocator
============================

yupiter allocates from a private static arena of YUPITER_HEAP_SIZE
bytes (4096 by default).  The heap never asks the OS for memory, so it
works freestanding.  Maximum loss on leaked pointers is the arena size;
accounting still reports it.

Not thread-safe.


Public API
----------

yupiter_malloc, yupiter_free, yupiter_realloc: standard semantics.
yupiter_malloc_safe, yupiter_free_safe, yupiter_realloc_safe: checked
variants that report failure instead of aborting.
yupiter_free_checked, yupiter_realloc_checked: status-returning variants.
yupiter_heap_live_bytes, yupiter_heap_live_blocks,
yupiter_heap_capacity: accounting used by tests.

The authoritative contract is the comments in include/yupiter.h.


Sizing
------

YUPITER_HEAP_SIZE is defined in include/yupiter_mem.hxx, default 4096.
Must be a plain decimal number, at least 64.  Static assertions reject
invalid values.  Tests query yupiter_heap_capacity and shape scenarios
to fit.


Layout
------

One contiguous run of blocks.  Each block: header then payload.  Header
rounded up to 16 bytes; payload sizes are multiples of 16.  Requests
rounded up the same way.  Free blocks carry a next pointer; allocated
blocks do not.

Allocation scans free blocks first-fit; release coalesces adjacent free
blocks.  Realloc allocates, copies, frees.